title: 'statement-store: move the submit index to disk with bounded caches'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Stage 2b of the statement-store index refactor (#10910). The submit index (per-account
    quota accounting) now lives on disk next to the statements, with bounded in-memory caches
    on top. Store memory usage no longer grows with the number of stored statements or
    accounts, and startup no longer reads statement bodies, so it stays fast for large
    stores. Existing databases are migrated automatically on first start.
crates:
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: minor
